{"kind":"report","text":"Approved: archive fixed-parent fix at exact head 2c2980bc0017df80f8197e2b4a383c5babf2e807, tree 3b959b35a13ee0a9e8aebffd593c6b75c8704c83 (review request 40a41e1e, promise 98d6cd18, implementation fc2548ae / 28cdea0d). This head is the sole child of d51c9356, which I reviewed in bc2226d0 with one required documentation finding (F1). F1 is fixed. Everything else in that review carries over unchanged, because no code, test, seal or evidence byte differs. The head satisfies request fc2548ae as amended by planner rulings 63a9216f and e6e456e4. Its evidence meets the four continuation conditions that planner ruling b01b27bd confirmed for this head. It may land. Deployment is planner-owned.\n\nRead order: I read the primary, notes/implementation/2026-10-24-archive-fixed-parent.md (artifact 98b0f884), first and in full, then the diff from d51c9356.\n\nHead binding. Request 86c894ed named 9aeaf427, and the builder then amended that commit. 2c2980bc has the same parent (d51c9356), message and tree (3b959b35); only the committer timestamp differs. The builder superseded 86c894ed and published fresh artifacts at 2c2980bc that rest only on the implementation promise (40a41e1e). This review is bound to 2c2980bc. It uses bc2226d0 only as the record of what I checked at d51c9356, not as a basis for these artifacts.\n\nWhat changed. git diff d51c9356..2c2980bc changes exactly one path, the primary note (4 insertions, 4 deletions). Every other blob is byte-identical to d51c9356, so the code and tests are still those of the tested b86df6e5 (tree 397762ef). Under docs/testing.md:597, no new gate is needed.\n\nF1 fixed. Each figure below matches post-gate-repair/measurements.json and measurement-summary.md, and my own subtraction from the unchanged caps (64 nodes, 4,194,304 metadata, 67,108,864 input work):\n- Grow cohort: maxima of 57 nodes, 3,566,747 metadata and 62,328,993 input work leave margins of 7, 627,557 and 4,779,871. The note says input work is about