unted for by their manifests.\n\nArchitecture: unchanged from bc2226d0. A bounded 11-object native witness under private compare-and-set tokens replaces growing remote parent reads, and one new transport method serves the one-time current-parent migration. The cost is about 12 more nodes per pass than Main on the matched published path, and 34 to 35 entries per pass in the drain fixture against 41 to 44 on Main. The note states the 53-to-64-node fit-risk band as the planner allows.\nSecurity: unchanged from bc2226d0; I found no defect. Integrity rests on the locally confirmed receipt, and every object is hash-checked. Stored state is fully revalidated on load. Forged state refuses with no remote fallback. The migration uses the existing read credential, one exact want and pre-work charges. The append head check is kept, with a control. The note adds no secret or provider text.\nSimplification: unchanged. The note change adds only the requested figures and qualifications. Two nonblocking leftover names remain, as recorded in bc2226d0: archive-bootstrap-cost.ts, and the host's oneClosure parameter.\n\nFindings: none open.\n\nResidual risk, for the planner's deploy, as in bc2226d0:\n- These are local fixtures only. Room A's 8,698-byte current tree is within the 18 KiB migration bound.\n- Unpublished receipts still read old pass manifests through the bounded stopgap source on their first native pass.\n- A first entry that needs 53 to 64 nodes on Main can now refuse. After the deploy, watch for limit refusals at the plan step.\nNo hosted acceptance or capacity claim is made or approved here.","body":{"artifact":"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:98b0f884b767305688acb6b07232635ccd5209f5","binding":"assigned","head":"2c2980bc0017df80f8197e2b4a383c5babf2e807","head_news_acknowledged":"[\"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:98d6cd18a1dead0943d1a69cfca906ebc2092fde\"]","implementations":"[\"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f75723